# Auto-Update Implementation Plan (rust-api-auto-update)

This plan outlines the steps to implement an automatic update mechanism for the Activity Monitor Agent.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The update process requires the agent to replace its own binary and restart. On Windows, this involves interacting with the Service Control Manager (SCM) or using a helper script if running as a user process.

> [!WARNING]
> Only the **Session 0 (Service)** agent will be responsible for performing the update to ensure it has the necessary administrative permissions to replace files in the installation directory.

## Proposed Changes

### Server API (Rust + Axum)

#### [MODIFY] [api.rs](file:///c:/Dev/Monitorv3/server/src/api.rs)
- Add a new public route: `GET /api/agent/update-check`.
- This endpoint will accept `version`, `os`, and `arch` parameters.
- It will return JSON containing:
  - `latest_version`: The most recent version string.
  - `download_url`: Link to the binary.
  - `checksum`: SHA-256 hash of the binary.

### Client Agent (Rust)

#### [NEW] [updater.rs](file:///c:/Dev/Monitorv3/agent/src/updater.rs)
- Implement `check_for_updates(current_version: &str)` function.
- Implement `apply_update(download_url: &str, checksum: &str)` function.
- **Windows Implementation**:
  - Download new binary to `agent.exe.new`.
  - Verify checksum.
  - Spawn a temporary batch file `update_restart.bat` that stops the service, replaces the file, and restarts the service.
- **Linux/macOS Implementation**:
  - Use `std::fs::rename` to replace the binary (on Unix, you can replace a running executable's file).
  - Signal systemd or supervisor to restart.

#### [MODIFY] [main.rs](file:///c:/Dev/Monitorv3/agent/src/main.rs)
- Spawn an `auto_update_task` that runs every 6 hours.
- This task will only execute if `is_running_in_session_0()` is true.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Mock the server update endpoint and verify the agent detects a "new" version.
- Verify checksum validation logic.

### Manual Verification
1. Bump the version on the server.
2. Observe the agent logs for "New version detected".
3. Verify the agent successfully restarts and reports the new version.
